WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.770
Speaker 1: Donald Trump announced yesterday
in a second disgusting video that on day one

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:12.400
of his next presidency, if he is to get one,
he will violate the Constitution of the United

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.549
States.

00:00:13.549 --> 00:00:18.200
Trump loves the Constitution just like he
loves American flags and law and order and

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.710
all of these different things.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:24.519
Trump loves the Constitution, and many of
his followers see it almost like a sacred

00:00:24.519 --> 00:00:26.280
religious document.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:33.271
And yet, Trump says on day one of his presidency,
if he is inaugurated in January of 2025, he

00:00:33.271 --> 00:00:40.550
will sign an executive order ending birthright
citizenship as guaranteed by the 14th Amendment

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.210
to the Constitution of the United States.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:48.079
Here is Donald Trump looking admittedly a
little confused.

00:00:48.079 --> 00:00:51.059
Not clear he knows where he is or what he's
saying.

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:52.550
Take a listen to what he says.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.399
Speaker 2: Plan to secure the border.

00:00:54.399 --> 00:00:59.880
On day one of my new term in office, I will
sign an executive order making clear to federal

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:06.760
agencies that under the correct interpretation
of the law going forward, the future children

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:10.299
of illegal aliens will not receive automatic
U.S. citizenship.

00:01:10.299 --> 00:01:11.890
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:16.760
Now, he says there according to some interpretations
of the law.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:22.600
If you can find me serious legal experts who
believe that birthright citizenship could

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:27.500
be denied as written in the 14th Amendment,
please send me that.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:32.720
Because all of the research I did this morning
matches up with my prior discussions with

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.950
legal experts on the matter, which is it is
very clearly part of the 14th Amendment.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:41.570
Now, I want to focus in on one particular
aspect of this.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:47.210
The right wingers cheerleading this idea and
birthright citizenship and anchor babies as

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.950
they like to call them.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:53.799
Those right wingers should be very careful
about the unintended consequences that Trump

00:01:53.799 --> 00:01:56.060
trying to do this could have.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:03.149
First of all, it does appear it would violate
the Constitution and the Supreme Court precedent,

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:09.929
which established that there is a fundamental
right to citizenship if born in the United

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.239
States.

00:02:11.239 --> 00:02:17.790
Right wingers claim to worship that document
as a religious text, and indeed, it appears

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.920
as though this is a fundamental right.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:29.410
If they were to attempt this, it would be
potentially years and years and years of legal

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:33.610
conundrum, we might call it.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:40.800
And in the immediate, it would much more quickly
increase the undocumented population in the

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.770
United States, which they claim to want to
reduce.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:46.019
This is a really important thing.

00:02:46.019 --> 00:02:53.440
If Trump ends birthright citizenship going
forward, then you are going to have a situation

00:02:53.440 --> 00:03:02.740
where babies will be born here, will immediately
be undocumented, presumably subject to deportation,

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:12.080
and it will so instantly clog up and gum up
immigration processes that because you will

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:17.739
all of a sudden see authorities tied up with
looking at deporting newborn babies.

00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:22.870
You actually might you know, they say that
we really care about criminal aliens, the

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:28.860
people committing crimes, etc., to the extent
that they exist and they do to a degree, but

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:34.900
just not to the degree that Donald Trump says
you are going to get in the way of actually

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:41.920
locating and deporting those individuals who
are only not only undocumented, but have committed

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.550
crimes because you are going to be focusing
on trying to deport newborn babies.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:50.260
They are going to make the problem they want
to fix worse.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.950
Secondly, it will impact the American economy.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:55.569
It will reduce the labor force.

00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:57.189
It will reduce the tax base.

00:03:57.189 --> 00:04:01.940
It will reduce consumer demand by just getting
rid of people and their families, even if

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.989
they're babies and they're not spending their
own money.

00:04:04.989 --> 00:04:09.690
You are going to push them as well as potentially
parents out of the United States.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:13.000
You will reduce the tax base, reduce the labor
force and reduce consumer demand.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.930
That's not good for the economy.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:17.470
Years of legal challenges will also come with
them.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.940
It will bring with them huge financial costs.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:25.830
These claim to be fiscal conservatives, but
of course it will be extraordinarily expensive

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:30.060
and it will destroy international image of
the United States.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.470
Now, that's not anything new.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:36.979
You might remember that Gallup global surveys
about global opinion about the United States

00:04:36.979 --> 00:04:41.650
bottomed out when Trump was president has
fortunately started to recover since Joe Biden

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:43.169
became president.

00:04:43.169 --> 00:04:50.950
But again, the United States, for all of our
faults, the United States has been seen.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:55.520
Generally not every part of the United States,
but generally the United States has been seen

00:04:55.520 --> 00:05:01.020
as a nation that embraces immigrants, offers
opportunity to those born within its borders.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:06.180
And if you end birthright citizenship, particularly
in this vindictive way, you're going to tarnish

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:12.650
that image, and then that will make it more
difficult to continue having the exact same

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:15.860
relationships diplomatically with our long
term allies.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:20.229
There will be other countries affected by
the policy change on and on and on.

00:05:20.229 --> 00:05:27.390
And there are question marks as to what such
a decision by Trump would do to national security

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:28.390
efforts.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:32.139
And what I mean by that is that birthright
citizenship has implications for national

00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:37.800
security because it says, okay, if you're
born here, you have a vested interest in the

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:40.039
country, you get citizenship.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:42.050
That creates a tie.

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:48.440
If you end birthright citizenship for people
born here, you can create all sorts of different

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:50.090
security issues.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:55.050
Legal gray areas, raise questions about rights
and obligations of individuals within the

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.270
country.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:59.340
It's extraordinarily problematic in a number
of different ways.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:03.240
Now, do we believe Trump will actually do
this on day one of his presidency?

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:04.240
I don't know.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.330
I mean, I genuinely don't know.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:08.000
Trump says a lot of things.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.580
He told us in August of 2020 that we were
two weeks away from receiving his new health

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:12.950
care plan.

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:13.950
I'm still waiting for it.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.319
I'm really curious what would be in there.

00:06:15.319 --> 00:06:17.169
Maybe he met August of 2024.

00:06:17.169 --> 00:06:19.300
I don't know at this point in time.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.330
But will Trump actually do it?

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.330
Unclear.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:23.349
Would this be a good idea?

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:24.349
No.

00:06:24.349 --> 00:06:26.500
Would it even be constitutional?

00:06:26.500 --> 00:07:34.520
Probably not.

